        <item>
            <title>0.15.23</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 12:11:24 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>184</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.23</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Recordings take much less disk. Retained audio (your mic, the far end, and the playback mix) is now stored as 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM — exactly what transcription and playback use — instead of the far larger 44.1/48 kHz stereo float32 the capture produced. Existing recordings are compacted in the background on launch. Combined with the removed silent backup track, a reported ~940 MB meeting drops to roughly ~110 MB with no change to transcript or playback quality.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
